Z||000003||mrfixit58||04-26-2001||05:21 PM||||As has been said many times... "you get what you pay for". If the price is cheap, expect to spend more time refining the product before it's painted. It's best to arrange with the supplier -- up front -- that if the product you buy is not to your liking you can return it for a full refund. Then, if it's fit and finish is too much for the buyer to complete, there's no hard feelings. With the proper feedback, I would hope that the manufacturer will improve their product. <P>This manufacturer is trying very hard to make new items for our beloved Fieros. He has attended many of the Suncoast Fiero meetings and asked us what we would like to see in the way of future products. Some of his current offerings are a direct result of the feedback I have given him based on what I've heard HERE. As his company continues to develop, he plans on making more unique items.<P>It's true that he is in the process of moving his business. I would ask that you give him some time to make things right. I would hate to see another "Where's my Money?" thread. Personally, I believe unprovoked product bashing is unproductive. If the product isn't what you were promised or expected, send it back and buy someone else's. That will go father to correcting a problem. <P>Yes, you are entitled to your opinion of fit and finish. Yes, it's an open forum and you free to express your opinion. All I am saying is, be careful not to "kill the goose that is laying the golden egg". <P>Flame suite ON,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
